  values
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'If two forces act along the same straight line but in opposite directions, the magnitude of their resultant is found by which operation?', '["Addition","Subtraction","Multiplication","Division"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '869e5f3dc32d', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'When vectors act at a certain angle instead of being parallel, which method must be drawn to add them?', '["Algebraic addition","Head-to-tail rule","Direct subtraction","Simple linear scale"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, 'b84955e8831d', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'If an object is moving in a straight line at a completely constant speed, what is the net external force acting on it?', '["Max force","Variable force","Zero force","Infinite force"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '02fb2e8e03e7', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A passenger falls backward when a bus accelerates rapidly from rest. Which property explains this?', '["Weight","Velocity","Friction","Inertia"]'::jsonb, 'D', 1, 'db687c2a3d44', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'If you want to change the state of rest or uniform motion of any object, what type of force is required?', '["Balanced force","Unbalanced force","Internal force","Zero force"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '4ae9cdb9d179', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'Which physical quantity is the direct, fundamental measure of a body''s inertia?', '["Weight","Speed","Mass","Volume"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '07789b964b30', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A net, completely unbalanced external force acts continuously on a macroscopic object. Which inherent property of this moving object will always undergo a change?', '["Velocity","Intrinsic mass","Structural inertia","Gravitational weight"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, '0acfae4d9196', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A player catches a fast baseball with rigid, locked arms and stationary hands instead of pulling them backward during the catch. Which physical variable increases dramatically because of this action?', '["Average impact force","Total momentum change","Total net impulse","Total duration of impact"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, 'cf6466641de8', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A massive block of ice rests on a completely frictionless frozen lake. A heavy stone is thrown horizontally at the block and sticks to it upon impact. Right after the collision, what happens to the total kinetic energy and the total linear momentum of the two-body system?', '["Both stay constant","Momentum drops, energy stays","Momentum stays, energy drops","Both values drop"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '06285958eeba', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'According to Newton''s third law of motion, action and reaction forces always act on which bodies?', '["The same body","Different bodies","Only heavy bodies","Only moving bodies"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '49360b44bf2b', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'When a person jumps out of a small boat onto a dock, the boat moves backward. The backward motion of the boat is called what?', '["Action force","Inertia force","Reaction force","Gravitational force"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '7df10b70c6e1', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'An exceptional marksman fires a heavy armor-piercing bullet from a standard rifle. The bullet accelerates inside the barrel in 0.005 seconds, while the rifle''s recoil velocity is felt by the marksman''s shoulder over the exact same time frame. Why does the marksman''s body easily withstand the recoil?', '["Rifle feels less force","Marksman''s mass resists acceleration","Bullet loses its momentum","Barrel eliminates the reaction"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '8aa4d92dcfbf', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'Why do action and reaction forces never cancel each other out during motion?', '["They are unequal","They act simultaneously","They act on different objects","They act along different lines"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '1ca20eaff260', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'When a heavy stone is dropped, the Earth pulls the stone down. What does the stone do to the Earth?', '["Nothing","Pushes it away","Pulls it up equally","Pulls it up less"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, 'fc6b8437fc51', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A large, massive astronaut floating completely at rest in deep space throws a small, light wrench away from himself. Immediately after the throw, how do the magnitudes of their linear momentums compare?', '["Astronaut has more momentum","Wrench has more momentum","Both momentums are equal","Both momentums are zero"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, 'a853fccdefa8', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'During the firing of a bullet from a rifle, why does the heavy rifle recoil with a much smaller velocity than the bullet?', '["It experiences less force","It has a larger mass","Its momentum is lost","Friction stops it completely"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '69fb90b26cf6', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'If a gas-propelled rocket accelerates upward in the complete vacuum of outer space, what does it push against to move forward?', '["Atmospheric nitrogen","Its own ejected exhaust gases","Planetary magnetic fields","Surrounding cosmic dust"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, 'a930efce498c', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'What does the mathematical area under a Force-versus-Time graph directly represent?', '["Acceleration","Linear momentum","Structural inertia","Impulse"]'::jsonb, 'D', 1, '4f8391458d78', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'If a system is strictly classified as an "isolated system," what must be the value of the net external force acting on it?', '["Maximum","Constant and positive","Exactly zero","Dynamically variable"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '513b98032ab3', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'According to Newton''s second law written in terms of momentum, the net force acting on an object equals what?', '["Total momentum","Rate of change of momentum","Product of momentum and time","Initial momentum value"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '6b625de58fde', null),
